From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000019 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sf2000-linux <sf2000-linux@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 12:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: use fixed early TLB flush

The physical unit now reaches the "wired skip/read" marker. In the generated
code the next instructions still enter the generic local_flush_tlb_all()
feature path, reading current_cpu_data options and tlbsize before the first
TLB write marker can run.

The SF2000 bring-up profile already forces a 16-entry 4Kc-style TLB and has no
Linux-owned wired mappings at this point. Use a fixed 16-entry indexed flush
for this early path so it no longer depends on the generic feature branch.
Keep diagnostic calls outside the EntryLo-zero staging window by restoring an
invalid non-zero EntryLo staging value before emitting post-write markers.
---
 arch/mips/mm/tlb-r4k.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/mips/mm/tlb-r4k.c b/arch/mips/mm/tlb-r4k.c
index 01f9ce11e6fb..d742f1b62c39 100644
--- a/arch/mips/mm/tlb-r4k.c
+++ b/arch/mips/mm/tlb-r4k.c
@@ -86,6 +86,35 @@ void local_flush_tlb_all(void)
 	first_entry = entry;
 	sf2000_tlb_tick("tlb-flush-after-wired-read");
 
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MIPS_SF2000)) {
+		sf2000_tlb_tick("tlb-flush-before-first-write");
+		while (entry < 16) {
+			write_c0_entryhi(CKSEG0 + (entry << (PAGE_SHIFT + 1)));
+			write_c0_index(entry);
+			write_c0_entrylo0(0);
+			write_c0_entrylo1(0);
+			mtc0_tlbw_hazard();
+			tlb_write_indexed();
+			if (entry == first_entry) {
+				tlbw_use_hazard();
+				write_c0_entrylo0(1);
+				write_c0_entrylo1(1);
+				sf2000_tlb_tick("tlb-flush-after-first-write");
+			}
+			entry++;
+		}
+		tlbw_use_hazard();
+		write_c0_entrylo0(1);
+		write_c0_entrylo1(1);
+		sf2000_tlb_tick("tlb-flush-after-loop");
+		write_c0_entryhi(old_ctx);
+		htw_start();
+		flush_micro_tlb();
+		local_irq_restore(flags);
+		sf2000_tlb_tick("tlb-flush-done");
+		return;
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * Blast 'em all away.
 	 * If there are any wired entries, fall back to iterating
-- 
2.50.1
